INSERT INTO kb.chunks (doc_id, chunk_no, section, sap_refs, content) VALUES
('AU-CMP-KYC-001', 1, '1. Scope and risk-based approach', '{"scopes": ["counterparty_credit"]}'::jsonb,
$md$This standard applies to every counterparty of the Group (customers including copper refiners and smelters, suppliers and logistics providers) in every country of operation. No credit exposure, delivery or payment may be executed before onboarding is approved. Each counterparty receives a risk rating (low, medium or high) based on jurisdiction, ownership structure, product and payment channel. Onboarding must be re-validated every 24 months and immediately after a trigger event: change of ownership, sanctions alert, request for a credit limit increase, or a credit block in SAP.$md$),

('AU-CMP-KYC-001', 2, '3. Tax documentation: Form W-8BEN', '{"scopes": ["counterparty_credit"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Before activation, collect the IRS withholding certificate from every non-US counterparty: Form W-8BEN for individuals and Form W-8BEN-E for legal entities. Validate the legal name, country of incorporation, foreign tax identification number (TIN), treaty claim and signature date against the incorporation documents. A form is valid until 31 December of the third year after signature; an expired, unsigned or inconsistent form blocks onboarding and re-validation, and payments subject to US withholding must then be withheld at 30 %. Store the form in the counterparty file and record its validity in the SAP business partner.$md$),

('AU-CMP-KYC-001', 3, '4. Anti-money laundering (AML) validation', '{"scopes": ["counterparty_credit"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Screen the counterparty, its directors and every ultimate beneficial owner holding 25 % or more against the UN, OFAC, EU and Australian (DFAT) sanctions lists, politically exposed persons (PEP) databases and adverse media. Red flags include payments from third parties, cash or cryptocurrency settlement, transit through high-risk jurisdictions and ownership that cannot be verified. Any unresolved hit stops the process; high-risk counterparties require enhanced due diligence approved by the Group Compliance Officer. Screening results are valid for 12 months.$md$),

('AU-CMP-KYC-001', 4, '6. Credit limits and blocked counterparties', '{"scopes": ["counterparty_credit"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Credit limits are approved by the Credit Committee according to the risk rating; limits above USD 5,000,000 require approval by the Board Credit Committee. When exposure (open receivables plus open orders) exceeds the approved limit, SAP credit management automatically blocks the counterparty for new sales orders and deliveries. To release the block, either collect the overdue receivables or obtain a temporary limit increase approved at the required level; in both cases KYC must be current (valid W-8BEN or W-8BEN-E and AML screening younger than 12 months). Document the decision in the SAP credit case and never bypass the block with manual deliveries.$md$),

('AU-CMP-KYC-001', 5, 'Annex BR. Brazil fiscal registration requirements', '{"scopes": ["counterparty_credit"]}'::jsonb,
$md$For counterparties in Brazil, the customer master record must contain the CNPJ (Cadastro Nacional da Pessoa Jurídica) of the establishment and its Inscrição Estadual (state tax registration, IE). Both fields are mandatory in SAP transaction XD01 (create customer) and the record cannot be saved without them; an IE recorded as ISENTO (exempt) requires a written justification from the tax department. Before creating or reactivating the customer, confirm that the CNPJ status is ATIVA at the Receita Federal and validate the IE in the state registry (SINTEGRA), because NF-e invoices cannot be issued against an invalid registration.$md$),

('AU-FLO-STR-003', 1, '1. Principle', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-REAG-4410"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Collector dosage must follow the head grade and mineralogy of the ore actually fed to flotation, not a fixed setpoint. Under-dosing a lower grade feed loses fine and composite sulfide particles to the tailings; over-dosing reduces selectivity, raises reagent cost and can depress concentrate grade. The reference collector is sodium isopropyl xanthate (SIPX), dosed to the conditioning tank ahead of the rougher bank.$md$),

('AU-FLO-STR-003', 2, '2. Dosage matrix by head grade', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-REAG-4410"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Apply the following xanthate (SIPX) dosage by head grade: 10 g/t when the head grade is 0.8 % Cu or higher; 12 g/t between 0.6 % and 0.8 % Cu; 15 g/t when the head grade drops below 0.6 % Cu. Never exceed 18 g/t without approval from the Group Metallurgist. A grade band change is confirmed only after two consecutive shift assays fall inside the new band; then adjust the dosage at the start of the next shift.$md$),

('AU-FLO-STR-003', 3, '3. Dose change procedure', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-REAG-4410"]}'::jsonb,
$md$1) Raise a management of change (MOC) record signed by the plant metallurgist with the assay evidence. 2) Change the dosing pump setpoint and verify the actual flow with a calibration cylinder (drawdown test) within 30 minutes. 3) Monitor rougher tailings grade, froth color and mass pull every two hours for the next 24 hours. 4) If the tailings grade does not improve after 24 hours, return to the previous dosage and escalate to the Group Metallurgist. Record every change in the shift log.$md$),

('AU-FLO-STR-003', 4, '4. Reagent inventory and consumption', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-REAG-4410"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Daily xanthate consumption (kg/day) = dosage (g/t) × throughput (t/day) / 1000. Example for a 40,000 t/day concentrator: 400 kg/day at 10 g/t and 600 kg/day at 15 g/t, a 50 % increase. Keep a minimum of 14 days of consumption on site at the current dosage and trigger replenishment as soon as coverage falls below that level, considering the supplier lead time. Store xanthate dry, ventilated and away from heat sources: wet or hot xanthate decomposes and releases flammable carbon disulfide (CS2).$md$),

('AU-FLO-STR-003', 5, '5. SAP posting of reagent consumption', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-REAG-4410"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Post the daily reagent consumption from the reagent depot to the flotation cost center with SAP transaction MIGO (goods issue, movement type 201), using the quantity measured by the dosing system. Reconcile physical and book stock weekly; differences above 2 % must be investigated before posting adjustments. After a dosage change, update the consumption forecast so that purchasing receives the new daily rate.$md$),

('AU-LIX-SOP-002', 1, '2. PLS flow optimization', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-ACID-9902"], "cost_centers": ["CC-LIX-01"]}'::jsonb,
$md$The pregnant leach solution (PLS) flow from the heap leach pads to the solvent extraction (SX) plant must be kept between 800 and 900 m³/h, with an irrigation rate of 10 to 12 L/h/m² on the active cells. Monitor PLS copper grade and pH every two hours: the target is 2.5 to 3.5 g/L Cu and pH 1.6 to 2.0. If the PLS grade falls below 2.5 g/L Cu for two consecutive readings, verify the irrigation distribution and the free acid concentration of the irrigation solution before increasing flow; increasing flow with low grade dilutes the SX feed and reduces copper transfer.$md$),

('AU-LIX-SOP-002', 2, '3. Acid concentration adjustment', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-ACID-9902"], "cost_centers": ["CC-LIX-01"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Free sulfuric acid in the irrigation (raffinate) solution must be held at 10 to 12 g/L H2SO4. Adjust the acid dosing pump setpoint in steps of no more than 0.5 g/L every 8 hours and confirm each step by titration two hours after the change. Never exceed 15 g/L: excess acid increases gangue acid consumption and gypsum precipitation that blinds the pad. With one acid dosing pump out of service, the remaining pump must not run above 85 % of its rated flow; reduce the irrigated area instead and record the change in the shift log. Wear acid-resistant suits, gloves and face shields at the dosing station.$md$),

('AU-LIX-SOP-002', 3, '5. Centrifugal acid pump disassembly', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-ACID-9902"], "cost_centers": ["CC-LIX-01"]}'::jsonb,
$md$1) Isolate the pump per the site lockout standard (electrical, hydraulic and chemical energy) and close and lock the suction and discharge valves. 2) Drain the casing, flush with water and neutralize with soda ash solution until the drain pH is between 6 and 8. 3) Remove the casing bolts and withdraw the back pull-out assembly with the lifting frame. 4) Inspect impeller, wear plates and shaft sleeve; replace the mechanical seal and impeller kit (P/N APX-450-SIK) whenever the seal has leaked acid. 5) Reassemble, torque the casing bolts to 180 N·m in a cross pattern and set the impeller front clearance to 0.5 mm. 6) Before handover, check the rotation direction and confirm vibration below 4.5 mm/s RMS during the first hour.$md$),

('AU-LIX-SOP-002', 4, '6. Post-storm inspection and restart', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-ACID-9902"], "cost_centers": ["CC-LIX-01"]}'::jsonb,
$md$After a tropical storm, flooding or lightning activity, treat every acid pump motor as wet until proven dry. Measure insulation resistance with a 1000 V DC megger: the minimum is 100 MΩ; below that value, dry the motor and repeat the test. Inspect terminal boxes and cable glands for water ingress, check bunds and drains for acid overflow, and verify that the pump base and anchor bolts were not undermined. Do not energize a pump with a failed insulation test or water in the terminal box; report the failure as a breakdown and keep the standby pump in service.$md$),

('AU-LIX-SOP-002', 5, '7. Work order management in SAP', '{"materials": ["SKU-BR-ACID-9902"], "cost_centers": ["CC-LIX-01"]}'::jsonb,
$md$Report every failure as a malfunction notification and create the corrective maintenance order in SAP transaction IW31, assigning the equipment and the leaching cost center that receives the costs. Before creating a new order, check in transaction IW38 that no open order exists for the same equipment, to avoid duplicate orders and double reservations. Reserve the spare parts on the order; if a spare has no stock, the reservation stays open and a purchase requisition is generated, so escalate critical spares with long lead times to Supply Chain on the same day. Close the order only after the post-repair checks are recorded.$md$);
